  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "The apparent cause of the FWP 'C' trip was a combination of the following factors: improper instrumentation thresholds during the last vendor preventative maintenance evolution in 2014, normal thrust bearing wear, and change in pump performance characteristics when the 'B' Main Feedwater Pump was secured. Engineering analysis determined that the thrust bearing wear detector 'Y' clearance was set low at some time in the past, most likely during major inspection as a part of RF21 in the Spring of 2014.",
    "cause_code": "B",
    "category": "Design/Manufacturing/Installation",
    "theme": "Miscalibrated thrust-bearing wear detector from 2014 maintenance masked normal bearing wear",
    "provisional": false
  },
